<channel|>Fizzlebang the Gnome trotted through the humid ferns of Stranglethorn Vale, his oversized hat tilting with every step. Beside him, his Succubus glided with a bored expression, occasionally snapping her whip at a passing raptor. 

As they approached a cluster of hostile trolls, Fizzlebang smirked. With a flick of his wrist, the Succubus cast Seduction, leaving the lead troll entranced and staring dreamily into her eyes. While the others scrambled in confusion, Fizzlebang unleashed a barrage of Chaos Bolts from the safety of the brush. "Efficiency, my dear!" he squeaked, adjusting his goggles. "Who needs a tank when you have a distraction?"

***

**Answer:**
Most players prioritize the Voidwalker because it provides **survivability and convenience**. While the Succubus deals more damage, the Voidwalker’s ability to taunt enemies allows the Warlock to cast spells without being interrupted or taking damage, eliminating the need to constantly kite or rely on health potions. [end of text]


